    "content": "Tigrayan forces took control of Alula Aba Nega Airport in Mekelle overnight, according to multiple reports. The facility had been under the control of federal police before the takeover.\n\nAn airport employee told AFP that staff attempting to report to work on Wednesday were turned away after a supervisor informed them that Tigrayan forces had seized the airport and that flights had been suspended. A security source at a Western embassy in Addis Ababa confirmed the takeover.\n\nThe seizure occurred just days after the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) announced a new alliance with six other armed groups. The coalition's stated aim is to overthrow Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed's government.\n\nThis development marks a significant escalation in the ongoing conflict between federal forces and Tigrayan fighters. The airport is a key transportation hub in the Tigray region.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the conflict in Ethiopia is of particular concern due to the large Somali population in the country and the broader regional instability it could provoke. Many diaspora members have family and business ties in Ethiopia and the Horn of Africa.\n\nRead the original report from Somalia Guardian here: https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/africa/tigray-forces-seize-mekelle-airport-ethiopia/",
